From 50ccfab8cbb370708056a9565904e8a2b81b2aee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:01:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add 'This Week Inbox' and generic inbox handling; improve
 Today archive toggle UX

### Motivation
- Introduce a separate "This Week Inbox" to the weekly widget to capture items scoped to the current week in addition to the existing "Next Week Inbox".
- Generalize inbox-related UI and logic so both inboxes share the same popover/mini-add/copy/clear behaviors.
- Make toggling archived items in the Today widget safer and more responsive by preventing duplicate requests and disabling controls while syncing with backend.

### Description
- Added UI for `This Week Inbox` in `widgets/this-week.html` including count, `Add` and `Show` buttons and integrated it into the preview modal and week copy/markdown exports by adding `thisInbox` to the persisted week state and formats.
- Reworked inbox code: introduced `activeInboxKey` and `inboxLabel` and replaced `nextInbox`-specific functions with generic `addInbox`, `toggleInbox`, `deleteInbox`, `clearInboxDone`, `copyInbox`, and unified popover/mini-add handling; updated positioning and popover title dynamically.
- Updated storage migration/normalization to include `thisInbox` by extending `emptyWeekState()` and `normalizeWeekState()` so older archives migrate gracefully.
- Preview handling updated to support `tx` (this inbox) and `nx` (next inbox) markers for toggling and deleting items with undo behavior in the week preview UI.
- Today widget improvements in `widgets/today.html`: badges in the preview are now interactive `button`s, added `pendingArchiveToggles` to avoid concurrent toggles, and implemented `toggleArchivedItem()` which updates local state immediately, disables the control while syncing, patches Supabase when `USE_SUPABASE` is enabled, and rolls back on error; added relevant event wiring to `previewBox` clicks.
- Minor UI/styling and accessibility enhancements for badges, mini modal title handling, and improved aria-labels.

### Testing
- Ran the repository build and lint checks with `npm run build` and `npm run lint`, both completed successfully.
- Ran the app smoke build and basic interaction smoke checks (UI build, popover open/close, add/toggle/delete flows) locally against the dev build and observed expected behavior; no automated unit tests were added or modified.

